---
title: Print form fields
---

# Inspection form

`\{% input %}` renders a print form field — a label above a ruled box, sized
by `maxlength`, with the type / length / value constraints noted beneath. It
is pure graphics, so it stays PDF/A-safe (PDF/A forbids the JavaScript that a
live-validated PDF field would need). The same tag renders as a native,
validated `<input>` on the web.

{% input name="serial" label="Serial number" type="text" required=true minlength=4 maxlength=24 /%}

{% input name="qty" label="Quantity received" type="number" required=true min=1 max=100 /%}

{% input name="email" label="Contact email" type="email" /%}

{% input name="date" label="Inspection date" type="date" /%}

{% input name="passed" label="Passed inspection" type="checkbox" required=true /%}

{% input name="notes" label="Notes" maxlength=60 /%}
